    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Churchill was a soldier and war correspondent before entering Parliament in 1900, and he crossed from the Conservatives to the Liberals and back, holding most of the great offices of state over half a century.</li><li>As prime minister from May 1940 he refused to seek a peace settlement after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, led a coalition government and built the alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> that defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in 1945.</li><li>A staunch imperialist, he has been criticised for his views on race and for decisions such as the bombing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> in the 1920s, his government's response to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> famine and the area bombing of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Churchill had a lateral lisp from childhood and worked on his pronunciation of the letter 's'; he turned the impediment into an asset, as when he called Hitler a &quot;Nar-zee&quot;.</p></aside>
    </section>

